WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:17.806
A long time ago, a famous outlaw lived in England.

2
00:00:19.207 --> 00:00:20.788
His name was Robin Hood.

3
00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:27.270
Robin and his band of merry men lived in the green woods of Sherwood Forest.

4
00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:31.192
The forest was near the town of Nottingham.

5
00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:35.246
Everyone in the countryside loved Robin and his men.

6
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.809
The outlaws always took care of those in need.

7
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.872
They robbed the rich and gave to the poor.

8
00:00:43.073 --> 00:00:46.316
They rarely said no to anyone in need who asked for something.

9
00:00:48.838 --> 00:00:51.840
This is the story of how Robin Hood became an outlaw.

10
00:00:54.082 --> 00:00:58.726
It began one day when the Sheriff of Nottingham announced an archery contest.

11
00:00:59.347 --> 00:01:03.494
Robin was only 18, but he was very proud of his skill as an archer.

12
00:01:03.514 --> 00:01:06.817
"I'm going to enter the contest!"

13
00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:08.078
he said to himself.

14
00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:12.862
One morning Robin chose his best bow and arrows.

15
00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:17.245
Then he set off from the town of Locksley.

16
00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:20.468
It was a beautiful day in May.

17
00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:25.472
Flowers bloomed in the fields and apple blossoms filled the trees.

18
00:01:27.054 --> 00:01:29.616
Birds chirped brightly and the sun felt warm.

19
00:01:30.992 --> 00:01:33.073
Robin whistled as he walked along.

20
00:01:34.713 --> 00:01:36.173
He was happy to be outdoors.

21
00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:41.175
On his way to Nottingham, Robin passed through Sherwood Forest.

22
00:01:43.115 --> 00:01:47.877
Suddenly he came upon a group of the king's men sitting under a tall oak tree.

23
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.017
The men were feasting and drinking.

24
00:01:53.498 --> 00:01:56.679
One man, with his mouth full of food, called out to Robin.

25
00:01:56.699 --> 00:01:59.040
"Hello, little lad!"

26
00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.300
he said, laughing.

27
00:02:01.884 --> 00:02:03.965
"I see you have your toy bow and arrows.

28
00:02:04.706 --> 00:02:05.846
Where are you taking them?"

29
00:02:07.087 --> 00:02:09.968
"Ha-ha!" The other men laughed too.

30
00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:12.070
Robin got angry.

31
00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.251
He didn't like being laughed at.

32
00:02:14.271 --> 00:02:17.292
"My bow and arrows are as good as yours!"

33
00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:18.353
he declared.

34
00:02:18.373 --> 00:02:21.795
"In fact, I'm on my way to Nottingham.

35
00:02:22.455 --> 00:02:25.857
I'm going to compete in the sheriff's archery contest."

36
00:02:27.318 --> 00:02:29.839
"Ha-ha! Listen to him!"

37
00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:31.020
said another man.

38
00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:33.670
"He's just a boy!

39
00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:37.193
But he thinks he can compete against real archers!"

40
00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:39.916
Robin fumed.

41
00:02:39.936 --> 00:02:43.940
"I'm very good at shooting.

42
00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:47.103
I can hit a target a thousand feet away!"

43
00:02:47.404 --> 00:02:48.304
he said boldly.

44
00:02:48.324 --> 00:02:51.187
The men roared with laughter.

45
00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:54.250
"Listen to him!"

46
00:02:54.551 --> 00:02:55.512
the first man said.

47
00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:59.309
"It's easy to boast when there is no target in sight!"

48
00:03:00.089 --> 00:03:02.390
At this Robin grew even angrier.

49
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:07.011
"Actually, I see a herd of deer in that clearing over there.

50
00:03:07.992 --> 00:03:11.192
I bet five pounds that I can kill the biggest one."

51
00:03:13.013 --> 00:03:17.234
"And I bet five pounds that you won't kill anything," the man replied.

52
00:03:19.215 --> 00:03:22.956
Robin picked up his bow and swiftly shot an arrow toward the herd.

53
00:03:23.488 --> 00:03:26.849
The finest deer in the herd dropped dead a second later.

54
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.931
"Ha!" Robin cried.

55
00:03:29.951 --> 00:03:31.972
"How do you like that shot?

56
00:03:32.692 --> 00:03:35.173
I wish I'd bet five hundred pounds!"

57
00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.654
The king's men weren't laughing anymore.

58
00:03:39.575 --> 00:03:41.096
Now they were angry.

59
00:03:41.976 --> 00:03:44.797
The man who'd lost the bet was the angriest of all.

60
00:03:44.817 --> 00:03:48.599
"You'd better get out of here!"

61
00:03:49.019 --> 00:03:51.260
the man said with a nasty snarl.

62
00:03:52.108 --> 00:03:56.350
"You just killed one of the king's deer and that's a very serious crime!"

63
00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.072
"Catch him!"

64
00:03:59.432 --> 00:04:00.332
cried another man.

65
00:04:00.352 --> 00:04:04.114
"No, let him go," said someone else.

66
00:04:04.134 --> 00:04:05.975
"He's just a boy.

67
00:04:06.056 --> 00:04:07.396
He won't hurt anyone."

68
00:04:08.197 --> 00:04:10.798
Robin stood silently, glaring at the men.

69
00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:14.540
Finally, he whirled around and stalked off.

70
00:04:15.581 --> 00:04:17.922
As he strode away, his blood boiled.

71
00:04:18.902 --> 00:04:21.684
He was still young and sometimes had a bad temper.

72
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.721
The man who'd made the bet was still furious too.

73
00:04:27.582 --> 00:04:30.603
This young stranger had embarrassed him in front of the others!

74
00:04:31.523 --> 00:04:34.825
Suddenly he sprang to his feet and grabbed his own bow.

75
00:04:35.805 --> 00:04:38.066
He sent an arrow whistling toward Robin.

76
00:04:39.006 --> 00:04:42.028
Luckily for Robin, the man's aim wasn't perfect.

77
00:04:42.888 --> 00:04:46.049
But his arrow still came very close to Robin's head.

78
00:04:49.131 --> 00:04:51.992
Robin spun around and lifted his own bow again.

79
00:04:52.732 --> 00:04:54.573
"You said I was no archer!"

80
00:04:54.893 --> 00:04:55.434
he cried.

81
00:04:55.454 --> 00:04:57.615
"I dare you to say that again!"

82
00:04:58.535 --> 00:05:02.798
He shot an arrow back at the man, and the man fell forward with a sharp cry.

83
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:11.522
As the other men gathered around their friend, Robin took off into the dense woods.

84
00:05:11.542 --> 00:05:13.363
"Go after him!"

85
00:05:13.763 --> 00:05:14.584
cried one man.

86
00:05:15.284 --> 00:05:18.066
But none of the men followed the bold young archer.

87
00:05:18.766 --> 00:05:22.068
They were all too afraid of his skill with his bow and arrow.

88
00:05:23.296 --> 00:05:26.557
Instead they turned back to their dead friend and lifted his body.

89
00:05:27.117 --> 00:05:29.418
They began to carry him toward Nottingham.

90
00:05:30.698 --> 00:05:34.739
As for Robin, all the joy had disappeared from that beautiful spring day.

91
00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.220
He hung his head.

92
00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:37.960
"What have I done?"

93
00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:38.921
he thought.

94
00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.881
"I wish I'd never seen those men.

95
00:05:43.502 --> 00:05:46.863
I wish I'd never raised my bow to shoot that first arrow!"

96
00:05:47.483 --> 00:05:50.184
Guilt and sadness filled young Robin Hood.

97
00:05:51.413 --> 00:05:54.386
"Yet there is nothing I can do now," he thought.

98
00:05:54.406 --> 00:05:56.295
"What is done is done."
